 xe Battlemage Intel Arc Pro B70: GuC stalls under sustained LLM inference — silent app hangs, no kernel fault (GuC 70.72.1, xe 1.1.0, kernel 7.0.0-42)

DISCLAIMER: This report was generated with Bionic running Qwen3.8-27B. I am not a developer, just a user that went down a very deep rabbit hole.
Date reported 11/12/2026

## Summary

Sustained LLM inference (27B model, 60k context, ~130–180k cumulative tokens) on an Intel Arc Pro B70 (Battlemage, device `e223`, stepping C0) reliably hangs the application within 1–2 hours. The hang is **silent in the kernel**: zero fault lines, no reset, no `TD flush timeout`. The app's main thread is blocked in `futex_do_wait` waiting for a GPU completion that never arrives. **The GuC firmware is provably alive during the hang** — its log ring keeps writing heartbeat events at ~20.8 ms intervals up to the moment of capture — but work is never completed/acknowledged. Recovery is a clean SIGTERM; no reboot, no GPU lock (on current stack).

We believe the stall is in the **xe driver ↔ GuC firmware path** (TLB invalidation / fence / completion acknowledgement), not in the userspace stack (llama.cpp/Bionic are witnesses only). Two related bug classes were observed; one is fixed by the kernel update, the other persists.


