## Bug A — `TD flush timeout` (appears FIXED by kernel 7.0.0-42, included for context)
On kernel 7.0.0-42: **0 occurrences** across multiple sessions.
On kernel 7.0.0-38 this system produced 12+ TD flush timeout faults — GuC failing to ack TLB invalidation (~300 ms wait in xe_guc_tlb_inval.c). Kernel 7.0.0-42 eliminated that logged class, but the same stall persists silently (Bug B below). 7.0.0-38 remains a known-bad kernel for reproducing the logged variant.

## Bug B — silent hang (OPEN, 4 recurrences)

| # | Time (2026)     | Uptime at fault | Kernel log | Recovery |
|---|----|--|--|---   |
| 1 | Nov 10 23:25    | <2 h            | silent     | SIGTERM |
| 2 | Nov 11 09:34    | <2 h            | silent     | SIGTERM |
| 3 | Nov 11 15:58    | <2 h            | silent     | SIGTERM |
| 4 | Nov 11 17:50:49 | ~58 min         | silent     | SIGTERM |

Cadence ≈ every 1–2 h of sustained generation / ~130–180k cumulative context tokens. Faults correlate with long-context, sustained-load operation; keep-model-loaded mitigates slightly.

### Forensics from freeze #4 (most complete capture)

1. **llama-server (PID 208064)**: main thread in `futex_do_wait` (syscall 202), wchan `futex_do_wait`, **no `xe_drm_ioctl` anywhere on kernel stack** → the GPU operation was submitted and is waiting for a completion/fence that never signals; the app is simply parked on a futex for its worker. GPU fds held: `renderD129` (GT1, opened 16:53), `renderD128` (GT0), plus inherited `renderD129` from the host app.
2. **`dmesg -T` tail (400 lines) at freeze time: zero driver fault lines.** This is the 4th kernel-silent occurrence.
3. **GuC log ring (first non-empty capture, `guc_raw_1794444654.bin`, FSLG format)** — decoded:
   - Layout: 112-byte header; events = 20 B = `[TSC u32][flags u32=0][code u32][w3 u32][w4 u32]`; TSC at ~19.2 MHz.
   - **GT1: 1668 events, TSC 100% monotonic, span 19.918 s (0x846ad8fa → 0x9b3620e3)**. The ring ends **at capture time** → the GuC was still logging while the app hung.
   - **Tail cadence: repeated ~20.8 ms events** (21.08 / 20.85 / 20.82 ms) — a live heartbeat loop.
   - **Periodic ~1.9–2.3 s log gaps** (at events 85, 162, 736, 1511, 1658 of 1668) — recurring 2 second stalls visible *inside* the GuC's own timeline, ~every ~2 s.
   - **Repeating 92–93 cycle motif** (≈0.21 s period) of GuC-internal event codes: `0x10514` (args 0–6), `0x503`, `0x10516`×2, `0x502`, `0x4b2`, `0x4e0` (arg `0x7000`), `0x4df`, …
   - `0xdeadbeee` sentinel in the data field: 235× (GT1), 92× (GT0) — no-data entries.
   - **GT0: 280 events, 100% monotonic, span only 0.145 s** (smaller buffer) — also live at capture.
   - Interpretation: **the GuC is not dead and is not silently frozen — it is spinning a periodic background loop and still writing logs while host work (fences/TLB/completions) is never completed.** Event-code semantics are defined only in GuC firmware source (kernel ABI headers define only buffer layout); Intel can map `0x10514/0x503/0x10516/0x502/0x4b2/0x4e0/0x4df/0xdeadbeee` directly.
 

